<LegalPage title="Privacy Policy | TrueLine Finishes" description="How TrueLine Finishes collects, uses and protects the details you send through the quote form, by phone, email or WhatsApp, and your rights under UK law." h1="Privacy Policy" page="privacy" lead="How TrueLine Finishes looks after the details you send us.">
  <p>Last updated: 5 November 2026.</p>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>TrueLine Finishes is a painting and decorating business run by Brandon Dawson. Brandon Dawson is responsible for the personal information described in this policy (the "data controller"). You can contact him about anything in this policy by email at <a href="mailto:Brandon@truelinefinishes.com">Brandon@truelinefinishes.com</a> or by phone on 07949 484274.</p>
  <h2>What information we collect</h2>
  <p>When you use the quote form we collect the type of work, whether you are a home owner or a tenant, your postcode, your short description of the job, your name, your phone number and your email address. The form also records the page you sent it from.</p>
  <p>When you call, email or message us on WhatsApp we keep what you tell us about the job and your contact details so that we can reply.</p>
  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To reply to your enquiry, talk the job through with you and give you a quotation.</li>
    <li>To arrange and carry out any work you ask us to do, and to keep the records that go with it.</li>
    <li>To keep the quote form secure and free of spam.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your details to third parties, and we do not use them for marketing unless you ask us to.</p>
  <h2>Our lawful basis</h2>
  <p>We use your information because you have asked us for a quotation or for work (taking steps at your request before entering into a contract, and performing that contract), and for our legitimate interest in running the business and answering enquiries. Where the law requires us to keep records, we do so to meet that legal obligation.</p>
  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>Your form submission is processed by an enquiry form service that receives it on our behalf and delivers it to us by email. Our email and phone providers handle messages in the normal way. These providers act on our instructions and may not use your information for their own purposes. We do not share your information with anyone else unless the law requires it.</p>
  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>We keep enquiry details for as long as we need them to answer your enquiry and, if you go ahead, to carry out the work and keep the business records the law requires. Enquiries that do not lead to work are deleted when they are no longer needed.</p>
  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under UK data protection law you can ask for a copy of the information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, ask us to delete it, or object to how we use it. To do any of these, contact Brandon using the details above. If you are unhappy with how we have handled your information you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at ico.org.uk.</p>
  <h2>Cookies and embedded content</h2>
  <p>This website does not use analytics or advertising cookies. Some pages show content from other websites, such as videos and a map. How that works is explained in our <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top shows when it was last changed.</p>
</LegalPage>
